 "text": "In 1935, crowds were watching a tiger shark at a Sydney aquarium when it threw up a human arm. Yes. In front of everyone. Police noticed two things. The arm had a tattoo of two boxers. And it hadn't been bitten off. It had been cut off. With a knife. The tattoo led them to James Smith, a former boxer who'd gone missing. This wasn't a shark attack. It was a murder… and the shark was just the delivery service. Police arrested a suspect. A key witness was about to testify, and then he was found shot dead in his car. The suspect was acquitted. The body was never found. The only witness who ever saw the evidence… was a shark.",
